rt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 84, lines 53-51"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on April 19, 2023."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 35-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 35-19"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["the side that brought the case wants the Court to require proof of specific intent for true threat convictions.","The state wants the Court to allow convictions based on knowledge or recklessness."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 108, lines 31-35","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 108, lines 31-35"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 51, lines 13-53","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 51, lines 13-53"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 65, lines 39-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 65, lines 39-49"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 84, lines 53-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 84, lines 53-51"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["the side that brought the case argues that categorical speech exceptions must be narrowly defined and historically settled.","The state argues that true threats have always been prosecuted without a specific intent requirement."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 108, lines 31-35","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 108, lines 31-35"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 51, lines 13-53","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 51, lines 13-53"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 65, lines 39-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 65, lines 39-49"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 84, lines 53-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-138_986b.pdf","page_label":"file page 84, lines 53-51"}]},{"heading":"What the justices asked","paragraphs":["Justice Thomas asked why true threats receive more protection than obscenity.","Justice Alito asked if knowledge suffices when purpose is not required."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcr